## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design content-based routing, with strict per-record validation and multi-stream fan-out. Emphasizes end-to-end tracing, fault handling, and test strategy in a realistic, beginner-friendly context.

## Key Concepts
- Content-based routing with multiple Kinesis streams
- Lambda validation of JSON schema and required fields
- Per-record tracing with AWS X-Ray
- Parquet writing to S3 and DLQ for invalid data
- LocalStack end-to-end testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-validator outline
function validate(record) {
  const hasFields = record.deviceId && record.ts && record.correlationId && typeof record.severity === 'number';
  const okSeverity = record.severity >= 0 && record.severity <= 100;
  return hasFields && okSeverity;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle backpressure if one stream lags significantly?
- What metrics would you emit to monitor data quality and latency?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical design of a privacy-conscious, end-to-end streaming pipeline that validates, masks, deduplicates, and persists data with observability.

## Key Concepts
- Kinesis Data Streams, Lambda, DynamoDB dedup, S3 Parquet storage, DLQ
- JSON schema validation, field-level masking of PII, correlationId
- Backfill strategy, LocalStack testing, basic observability (CloudWatch, X-Ray)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maskPII(record) {
  const r = {...record};
  if (r.email) r.email = r.email.replace(/[^@]+@/, '***@');
  if (r.phone) r.phone = r.phone.length > 4 ? r.phone.slice(0, 3) + '****' + r.phone.slice(-4) : r.phone;
  if (r.ssn) r.ssn = '***-**-' + r.ssn.slice(-4);
  return r;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the masking logic end-to-end, including replays?
- How would you ensure no PII leaks to DLQ or downstream sinks?
- How would you scale this to higher event rates or additional device classes?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a compliant, observable streaming pipeline with data masking in AWS DVA.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming patterns with Kinesis and Lambda
- Data redaction for PII in JSON payloads
- Parquet files in S3 with date/hour partitioning
- Error routing to DLQ and event auditing in DynamoDB
- X-Ray tracing and LocalStack test strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
function redact(payload){
  if(!payload) return payload;
  if(payload.email) payload.email = payload.email.replace(/[^@]+@[^.]+\.[^.]+/g, 'REDACTED');
  if(payload.phone) payload.phone = payload.phone.replace(/\d/g, 'X');
  return payload;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate redaction accuracy at scale?
- How would schema changes impact the validator and redactor?

